  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Seed Scoping Mission</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Ghanaian government has implemented a comprehensive seed policy, to develop a sustainable private sector-driven seed industry.However, challenges persist, such as limited uptake of certified seeds, financial difficulties for seed producers, insufficient storage facilities, weak distribution networks, and the prevalence of counterfeit seeds.Additionally, competition from neighbouring countries affects local markets. Only 5% of farmers have access to improved seeds from approved sources, and the formal sector struggles to produce sufficient quality and quantities of certified seeds. Poor retail conditions and limited knowledge among agro-dealers furthermore impact seed quality.The Netherlands Enterprise Agency (RVO) and the Netherlands embassy in Accra, Ghana are exploring opportunities for seed sector development in Ghana. Through a comprehensive study the current sector is mapped and opportunities for Ghanaian and Dutch private sector are identified.</narrative>
  </description>
